hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21499","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us: Musa ibn Uqbah informed us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Uqbah from Anas ibn Malik who said: I and Ubayy and Abu Talhah were sitting, and we ate meat and bread, then I called for ablution, so they said: Why do you perform ablution. I said: For this food we ate. So they said: Do you perform ablution from good things, one better than you did not perform ablution from it."
